{#-
  Sent when somebody asks to reset the password of an address that has no
  account. The forgot password page says "check your inbox" whatever the
  address, so it never shows who has an account; this email, which only
  the address's owner reads, says what is true. Context:
    register_url  the page to make an account on
    email         the address this is sent to, said back to them: many
                  people read several addresses in one mailbox
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}

{% block subject %}You do not have a Quill account yet{% endblock subject %}
{% block preheader %}Nobody has a Quill account with this address.{% endblock preheader %}

{% block body %}
{{ c.heading("No *account* here yet") }}
{{ c.paragraph("Hello,") }}
{{ c.paragraph("Somebody asked to reset the Quill password for this address, but nobody has a Quill account with it.") }}
{{ c.paragraph("If you meant to join a course, you can make an account now.") }}
{{ c.button("Register for Quill", register_url) }}
{{ c.small("This email was sent to " ~ email ~ ".") }}
{{ c.small("If you did not ask for this, you can ignore this email. Nothing has been changed.") }}
{% endblock body %}

{% block reason %}You are receiving this because a password reset was requested for this address on Quill.{% endblock reason %}

{% block text %}
Hello,

Somebody asked to reset the Quill password for this address, but nobody has a Quill account with it.

If you meant to join a course, you can make an account now.

Register for Quill: {{ register_url }}

This email was sent to {{ email }}.

If you did not ask for this, you can ignore this email. Nothing has been changed.
{% endblock text %}
